--- answer ---
Found it: `removeOldest` at simplelru/lru.go:170 evicts `c.evictList.Front()` — the newest entry — instead of `Back()` (the oldest). Items are pushed to the front and `MoveToFront` on hits, so the front is MRU and the back is LRU; `RemoveOldest`/`GetOldest` correctly use `Back()`.Fixed. The bug was in `removeOldest` at simplelru/lru.go:170: it removed `evictList.Front()` (the most recently used entry, since new items and cache hits go to the front) instead of `evictList.Back()` (the least recently used one). Changed `Front()` → `Back()`, matching `RemoveOldest`/`GetOldest`. Build, vet, and all package tests pass.